# ZZZ mods

Before you answer or edit anything about a Zenless Zone Zero mod, ZZMI, a character skin, oil, or OilSkinBoo, read `docs/zzz-mod-architecture.md` and follow it.

Live mods: `C:\Users\Ika\Desktop\zzz\FlairX Mod Manager\app\XXMI\ZZMI\Mods`

Game: `C:\Program Files\HoYoPlay\games\ZenlessZoneZero Game`

There is no `Glossify\` folder. The product is OilSkinBoo. Namespaces stay `Glossify*`. The packs share those namespaces, so enable one of `OilSkinBoo`, `油光布`, `OilSkinBoo-Glossify`, `油光布-全油化版`, or `OilSkinBoo-Skin`. Check which live folder is not `DISABLED_` before editing. A disabled copy is often stale. OilSkin 2 stays on beside that one pack. Do not edit `Matcap_ZZZ.ini`.

Phoenix Reffaella is the working character-mod shape. OilSkinBoo does not replace meshes.

- Put character maps in `Resource\ZZMI\...` and call `CommandList\ZZMI\SetTextures`. Do not assign `ps-t` for those maps. `ps-t0` is the shadow map.
- On a raw hash, one TextureOverride wins. `checktextureoverride` runs every match. A section that sets `match_priority` runs before one that leaves it unset, so Glossify `-1` runs before a mod at the default.
- Do not store a hash in a `persist` variable.
- Style is Numpad *, 0 through 7. 0 is off. Rebinds are the `[Key]` sections. Players change them in FlairX by pressing a key. `hotkeys.json` descriptions stay Menu, Face, Body, Style, Stronger, Weaker, Click. `$oilKeysEnabled` stays 0.
- Restore `$oilSkin` and `$oilStrength` before the next mesh calls OilSkin. Present already clears t124–t127.
- Do not draw a stock index list into a mod vertex buffer. Do not replace the face sheen with a body oil pass. Do not add a ShaderRegex that has no pattern.
- A black screen on this PC is commit exhaustion: 16 GB RAM, pagefile locked at 14 GB, `dwm.exe` `0xc00001ad`. Read System event 2004 before blaming an ini. Leave `.bin` caches. F10 cannot revive a closed game.
- `DISABLED_` is off. F10 reloads ini text. Ctrl+Alt+F10 wipes persisted values.

